A||||14||RZURCTN||Leather Power Seats?||||5
Z||000000||RZURCTN||11-22-1999||08:36 PM||||You see, here is the situation.  I have this 1979 Porsche 928 that is just sitting out in my drive way.  It's for sale, but I don't have all of the paper work ready for it yet.  It is in pretty sad shape, but it didn't cost me anything.  So whatever I sell it for will be pure profit.  Now, it has these real nice black leather bucket seats that are all electrical.  I've been having these naughty thoughts of putting them in my Fiero!  Doing that may decrease my selling value of the Porsche.  What should a guy like me do?  I need some valuable input here.  So if I could get some opinions from you guys and gals it would help ease my conscience.  Thanks!!   Ted.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||11-22-1999||08:54 PM||||Might as well put the seats in the Fiero since that is, by far, the better car.  If you'd rather leave them in the Porsche, let me know how much you want for it.  Maybe I'll buy it for the seats.  Just remember,  I know how much you paid for the car.:-))||||reg||1
Z||000002||DJRice||11-23-1999||09:02 AM||||Well, If you didnt pay for the car anyway, and its already in sad shape, I dont see where it would hurt anything to go ahead and pull the leather seats.<P>Also, If you get enough money for the Porsche, just order Mr. Mikes Leather Kit, or  go find a Camaro/Firebird with Power Leathers.  The seats in my 84 Fiero Came from an 97 Firebird.<P>In fact, heres an idea.  If the Fiero Seats are in decent shape, sell those and go get some cheap bucket seats from a bone yard and throw those in the Porsche.||||reg||1
Z||000003||RZURCTN||11-23-1999||10:55 AM||||I've been giving it a lot of thought lately, and I still can't decide.  There are a few people interested in it once I get the paper work straightened out.  They have already seen it with the seats in it.  If some one wanted to buy it for a parts car then that would be great.  But if they want it for restoration, then they will want the seats too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/rzurctn/Porsche2.jpg">   Like I said, it isn't much to look at, but those seats would be real nice in the Fiero.  And Monkeyman,  even though I didn't have to pay out the nose for the Porsche, I know what the value is for the car <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  "$15......going once!.....going twice!....Sold!...to the man with the funny looking monkey on his back! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">"<p>[This message has been edited by RZURCTN (edited 11-23-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-23-1999||07:57 PM||||I don't know that there's allot of sence in the power seats..... Is there enough room to actually move them much? I hardly ever move my seat. It's nearly straight up, and all the way back.<P>The Mr. Mikes stuff looks nice. How many people here have them? I think at least one does. I think he liked them. I was thinking about them, but I won't have the money for quite awhile. (Just changed jobs, no I wasn't planning to.)||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||11-23-1999||08:05 PM||||You ought to move to RI. If your car is over 10 yrs. old all you need is a bill of sale in order to get it registered.||||reg||1
